"""Render a readable index of the NE layout JSON; raw assets remain separate."""
from collections import Counter

def render(layout):
    h=layout['header'];s=layout['summary']
    rows=['# Executable layout and loader analysis','',
          'Generated by `python3 tools/ne_layout.py`. Input identity: `'+layout['input_sha256']+'`.','',
          'This is a static analysis image, not a runnable Windows process. Internal and imported addresses use synthetic selectors; no imported routine has been implemented. The original executable is unchanged.','',
          '## Header and initialization','',
          f"- NE header at file offset `0x{h['ne_file_offset']:x}`; linker header reports **{h['linker_version']}** (no exact linker build number).",
          f"- Windows executable; flags `0x{h['flags']:04x}` select multiple data instances and Windows GUI behavior. Expected Windows version field: `0x{h['expected_windows']:04x}`.",
          f"- Entry CS:IP: `{h['cs']:04x}:{h['ip']:04x}`; SS:SP header: `{h['ss']:04x}:{h['sp']:04x}`; automatic data segment: {h['autodata']}.",
          f"- Stack reserve: {h['stack_bytes']:,} bytes; local heap reserve: {h['heap_bytes']:,} bytes. SP=0 is a loader-placement request, not an assertion that execution begins with an empty stack at offset zero.",
          f"- DGROUP minimum including the requested heap and stack: {layout['initial_state']['initial_dgroup_allocation_before_allocator_rounding']:,} bytes before allocator rounding. Images contain static segment extents only; process startup/register setup remains runtime work.",
          '- No iterated-data, 32-bit, or module self-loading behavior is present. Moveable/discardable and preload attributes are retained below. A static image materializes even segments normally loaded on demand.',
          f"- {s['entry_records']} entry-table records, all moveable; {s['exports']} named exports. Export name/ordinal/address mappings are in `layout.json`.",'',
          '## Address model','',
          layout['analysis_model'],'',
          'A selector identifies a segment in this model; do not calculate a real-mode physical address as selector × 16. Use the per-segment files and the translation helpers in `tools/ne_layout.py`: `ne_to_file`, `file_to_ne`, `cv_to_ne`, and `selector_to_ne`. File translation returns no address for zero-fill. Synthetic import offsets are ordinal identifiers, not offsets in an actual DLL.','',
          '## Relocations','',
          f"- {s['relocation_records']:,} relocation records total: {s['address_fixup_sites']:,} address-patch sites after chain expansion, plus {sum(s['os_fpu_fixups'].values()):,} OS floating-point fixup records.",
          '- Internal references in this build relocate segment selectors. Imports use ordinal references; no by-name import relocation appears. Every unique ordinal has a Wine-export-map name annotation, with its reference URL retained. The ordinal is the binary evidence; the name is external annotation.',
          '- Non-additive chains are read from original bytes before patching. Every chain is bounds- and cycle-checked; tests confirm patch ranges do not overlap. This binary has no ordinary additive address relocation: the additive flag occurs on its OS fixups. The generic additive-pointer branch is tested separately.',
          '- Floating-point fixups retain the hardware-x87 instruction sequence, matching Wine’s hardware-FPU analysis policy. They are decoded and instruction-pattern checked, not applied as ordinary pointer additions. This does not emulate Windows’ software-FPU rewriting path.',
          f"- {len(layout['prologue_patches'])} exported prologue rewrite is recorded separately, following Wine’s NE loader handling. This is a stated loader-model choice, not a runtime observation.",'',
          '| FPU fixup subtype | Records |','|---:|---:|']
    for typ,n in sorted(s['os_fpu_fixups'].items(),key=lambda x:int(x[0])):rows.append(f'| {typ} | {n} |')
    rows+=['','## Segments','','| NE segment | Kind | File offset | Stored bytes | Static bytes | Moveable | Discardable | Preload |','|---:|---|---|---:|---:|---|---|---|']
    for seg in layout['segments']:
        rows.append(f"| {seg['segment']} | {seg['kind']} | `0x{seg['file_offset']:x}` | {seg['file_bytes']} | {seg['static_memory_bytes']} | {seg['moveable']} | {seg['discardable']} | {seg['preload']} |")
    rows+=['','## Imports','','| Module | Distinct imports |','|---|---:|']
    for mod,n in sorted(Counter(i['module'] for i in layout['imports']).items()):rows.append(f'| {mod} | {n} |')
    rows+=['','| Module | Ordinal | Annotated API |','|---|---:|---|']
    for imp in sorted(layout['imports'],key=lambda i:(i['module'],i['ordinal'] or 0)):
        rows.append(f"| {imp['module']} | {imp['ordinal']} | `{imp['name']}` |")
    rows+=['','## Resources','',
           'All 122 raw resources are extracted, including their NE allocation padding, and individually hashed. Dialogs, menus, accelerators, image-group references, and DIB metadata are decoded in `layout.json`. Graphics retain their original DIB/cursor/icon bytes; the `.bin` files are not standalone BMP/ICO containers. No string-table or VERSIONINFO resource is present. Text in dialogs and menus is decoded; game text stored elsewhere is later data-recovery work.',
           '', 'The three custom resource types (10000, 10002, 10004) remain opaque payloads with known boundaries and hashes; their formats belong to subsystem reconstruction. The raw resource index does not claim that their internal semantics have been recovered.','',
           '| Index | Type | ID/name | Bytes | Description |','|---:|---:|---|---:|---|']
    for r in layout['resources']:
        d=r['decoded'];desc=d.get('caption',d.get('decoding',''))
        if 'width' in d:desc=f"{d['width']} × {d.get('display_height',d['stored_height'])}, {d['bits_per_pixel']} bpp"
        rows.append(f"| {r['index']} | {r['type']} | {r['id']} | {r['bytes']} | {desc.replace('|','/')} |")
    rows+=['','## Whole-file accounting','',
           'Every file byte belongs to exactly one range in `layout.json:file_regions`; there are no unexplained nonzero gaps. Outside segments/resources/tables, remaining inter-region gaps are verified zero padding. The only trailing payload is the identified NB09 debug block and its trailer. Classification identifies storage roles, not the meaning of every instruction or data byte.',
           '', 'The DOS entry at file offset `0x200` executes a near CALL to `0x256`. That pops the message address into DX, sets DS=CS, uses DOS interrupt 21h/AH=09 to print “This program requires Microsoft Windows.”, and exits via AX=4C01h. No DOS relocations are present. DOS header size/page fields are retained as original metadata; their declared load extent overlaps NE metadata and must not be interpreted as a separate non-overlapping game overlay.',
           '', '## Validation evidence','',
           '- Tests partition the entire file, verify relocation-chain bounds and disjoint patch sites, and check every applied address fixup against its target.',
           '- `ReadIniSettings` at `0001:17cf` contains `9a ec 2a 41 09`: its selector word is a relocation-chain link. The internal fixup changes this to synthetic `9a ec 2a 28 10`, resolving the call to `0005:2aec`, the debug-record address of `FSerialAndEnvFromSz`.',
           '- The USER ordinal 1 record at file offset 118825 chains segment 5 offsets 29481 → 16395 → FFFF. Both sites resolve to synthetic `8020:0001`, annotated `MessageBox`.',
           '- The About dialog caption and 10 controls decode correctly. Every grouped icon/cursor points to an existing image resource; every dialog static-icon name resolves after case normalization.',
           '- Segments 5, 14, and 34 each have one final zero-filled byte; segment 37 has 17,236 zero-filled bytes. Translation and image checks explicitly cover these boundaries.',
           '- Data mapping independently agrees with `SetFileSeeds`: CodeView segment 69 offsets 0 and 4 map to DGROUP offsets 0x2272 and 0x2276, exactly the stores in the machine code for `lFileSeed1` and `lFileSeed2`. Both globals are in zero-fill.',
           '- These are byte-level and reference-implementation checks. No native Windows execution or independent decompiler import has been performed yet.','',
           '## Format references','',
           '- [Wine NE relocation, allocation, and prologue handling](https://github.com/wine-mirror/wine/blob/master/dlls/krnl386.exe16/ne_segment.c)',
           '- [Wine Win16 header definitions](https://github.com/wine-mirror/wine/blob/master/include/wine/winbase16.h)',
           '- [Wine packed Win16 dialog parser](https://github.com/wine-mirror/wine/blob/master/dlls/user.exe16/dialog.c)',
           '- Export-map URLs and downloaded-source hashes are retained in `references/win16_exports.json`. Loader-reference hashes are retained in `references/ne_sources.json`.','']
    return '\n'.join(rows)
